Runs for the proofs of the exchange core (branch proofs), on the build host in localhost/b8perf-lean with Lean v4.34.1.

Behaviour unchanged by the restructuring of the core (the two `partial def` loops as rounds of a certified `loopWhile`, commit ef6b4f3):
$ scp core-run.sh buildhost:<dir>/out/ && LEAN_HTTP_REMOTE_DIR=<dir> scripts/remote.sh bash out/core-run.sh <tag>
  base/     the core before the restructuring (git archive 6ae7b67, remote dir lean-http-proofs-base)
  loops/    the core after it (remote dir lean-http-proofs)
  Each has unit.txt, codec.txt, traces.txt, props-seed{1,2}.txt (200,000 random runs each), explore-10.txt.
  The outputs of base/ and loops/ are identical file for file, including the random runs' statistics.

The proofs, on the final tree (commit ff0b2de plus this file), from a fresh remote dir with no .lake (lean-http-proofs-final):
$ LEAN_HTTP_REMOTE_DIR=lean-http-proofs-final scripts/remote.sh bash -c 'lake build; lake env lean scripts/proof-axioms.lean; bash out/core-run.sh final'
  final/build.txt    lake build from scratch, LeanHttp.Exchange.Proofs among the modules built, no warnings
  final/axioms.txt   #print axioms for the 24 main theorems: each [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx
  final/*.txt        the same suites again; identical to loops/ file for file

Counterexamples, each run with `lake env lean --run` against the TestSupport library (lake build TestSupport first):
  gap0/        with gapMs := 0 (which Config.readGapMs allows), the checker's "a live exchange has a deadline
               ahead" fails right after begin: the write's deadline is now + 0.  With gapMs := 1 it holds.
  unreachable/ the single-step property "no head before the request head is written" does not hold for every
               exchange: from a hand-built state no run reaches (awaitingHead with nothing written), one step
               delivers a head.  The theorems therefore assume Inv, which Reachable.inv proves for every
               reachable exchange.
